WEBVTT

00:00:02.459 --> 00:00:03.890
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:04.208 --> 00:00:05.094
Sammy!

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:08.070
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can! Go!

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:13.090
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:13.794 --> 00:00:15.157
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.251
This is dad's book.

00:00:20.324 --> 00:00:22.051
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:22.596 --> 00:00:24.209
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:24.278 --> 00:00:25.391
Family business.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.936
Do you think Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.140
I can't do this alone.

00:00:28.955 --> 00:00:29.954
I'm driving.

00:01:17.196 --> 00:01:18.809
Can't keep kids out of this place.

00:01:19.059 --> 00:01:20.195
What is it anyway?

00:01:20.331 --> 00:01:21.716
I forgot you're not a local.

00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:22.898
You don't know the legend.

00:01:23.307 --> 00:01:24.079
Legend?

00:01:24.261 --> 00:01:26.197
Every town's got its stories, right?

00:01:26.629 --> 00:01:28.265
Ours is Roosevelt asylum.

00:01:28.947 --> 00:01:31.219
They say it's haunted with
the ghosts of the patients.

00:01:31.656 --> 00:01:32.542
Spend the night,

00:01:33.042 --> 00:01:34.768
Spirits will drive you insane.

00:01:41.287 --> 00:01:42.219
Hello?!

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.741
Police officers!

00:01:46.875 --> 00:01:48.239
Police officers!

00:01:56.793 --> 00:01:59.400
You tell me these kids
brought bolt cutters?

00:02:00.518 --> 00:02:01.291
Come on.

00:02:01.586 --> 00:02:02.450
Let's split up.

00:02:03.018 --> 00:02:03.949
All right.

00:02:18.149 --> 00:02:18.990
Hello?

00:02:47.939 --> 00:02:48.779
Hello?

00:03:12.385 --> 00:03:13.339
All right.

00:03:14.247 --> 00:03:15.496
Come on out.

00:03:43.909 --> 00:03:45.045
Kelly, you copy?

00:03:47.112 --> 00:03:47.976
Jeez!

00:03:48.794 --> 00:03:49.861
Where the hell you been?!

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:50.816
In there.

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:52.064
What was it? See anything?

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:56.094
No.

00:04:02.057 --> 00:04:05.055
This is patrol 1 4. We are
clear, we return to the station

00:04:25.016 --> 00:04:25.766
Hey.

00:04:33.955 --> 00:04:34.954
So, what?

00:04:35.795 --> 00:04:37.226
You're still not talking to me?

00:04:40.432 --> 00:04:41.227
Walt.

00:04:41.613 --> 00:04:43.340
I said I was sorry about before.

00:04:43.385 --> 00:04:45.135
How many times do I have to say it?

00:05:05.814 --> 00:05:08.267
No, dad was in California
last we heard from him.

00:05:08.835 --> 00:05:11.539
We just thought if he
comes to you for munitions,

00:05:11.771 --> 00:05:13.430
Maybe you've seen him
in the last few weeks.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.457
Just call us if you hear anything. Okay.

00:05:15.606 --> 00:05:16.504
Thanks.

00:05:17.464 --> 00:05:18.561
Caleb hasn't heard from him?

00:05:18.611 --> 00:05:19.284
Nope.

00:05:19.409 --> 00:05:21.654
Neither has Jefferson or pastor Jim.

00:05:22.078 --> 00:05:23.625
What about the journal?
Any leads in there?

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.297
No. Same last time I looked.

00:05:25.346 --> 00:05:26.868
Nothing I can make out.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.580
I love the guy, but I swear
he writes like freaking Yoda.

00:05:30.581 --> 00:05:32.076
And maybe we should call the feds,

00:05:32.226 --> 00:05:33.274
File a missing person's out.

00:05:33.275 --> 00:05:35.669
We talked about this. Dad would be
pissed if we put the feds on his tail.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:36.816
I don't care anymore

00:05:36.941 --> 00:05:38.959
After all that happened back in kansas,

00:05:39.009 --> 00:05:39.982
I mean...

00:05:40.232 --> 00:05:41.180
He should have been there, Dean.

00:05:41.181 --> 00:05:43.200
You said so yourself. You
tried to call him and nothing.

00:05:43.274 --> 00:05:44.272
I know.

00:05:44.719 --> 00:05:46.066
I loose my cellphone.

00:05:46.166 --> 00:05:48.012
You know, he could be
dead for all we know.

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:49.284
Don't say that.

00:05:49.609 --> 00:05:51.131
He's not dead. He's...

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:53.526
He's what? He's hiding? He's busy?

00:05:59.986 --> 00:06:01.183
I don't believe it.

00:06:01.807 --> 00:06:02.730
What?

00:06:06.477 --> 00:06:08.422
It's a-A text message.

00:06:09.619 --> 00:06:10.742
It's coordinates.

00:06:12.787 --> 00:06:14.659
You think dad was texting us?

00:06:14.855 --> 00:06:16.153
He's given us coordinates before.

00:06:16.203 --> 00:06:18.273
The man can barely work a toaster, Dean.

00:06:18.498 --> 00:06:19.845
Sam, this is good news.

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.341
It means he's okay, or alive.

00:06:21.541 --> 00:06:23.162
Was there a number on the caller I.D.?

00:06:23.212 --> 00:06:24.410
Huh, it said "unknown."

00:06:24.465 --> 00:06:25.737
Okay, well, where do
the coordinates point?

00:06:25.787 --> 00:06:27.060
That's the interesting part.

00:06:27.259 --> 00:06:28.706
Rockford, Illinois.

00:06:29.676 --> 00:06:30.874
Okay, and that's interesting how?

00:06:30.924 --> 00:06:33.717
I checked the local rockford
paper. Take a look at this.

00:06:37.082 --> 00:06:38.679
This cop, Walter Kelly,

00:06:38.903 --> 00:06:40.775
Comes home from his
shift, shoots his wife,

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:42.945
Then puts the gun in his
mouth, blows his brains out.

00:06:43.045 --> 00:06:45.140
Earlier that night,
kelly and his partner

00:06:45.141 --> 00:06:47.697
Responded to a call at
the Roosevelt asylum.

00:06:47.772 --> 00:06:50.291
Okay, I'm not following. What
does this have to do with us?

00:06:50.292 --> 00:06:53.235
Dad earmarked the same
asylum in the journal.

00:06:54.006 --> 00:06:55.254
Let's see.

00:06:56.875 --> 00:06:57.574
Here.

00:06:57.649 --> 00:07:00.292
"Seven unconfirmed
sightings, two deaths"

00:07:00.442 --> 00:07:01.889
Till last week, at least.

00:07:02.163 --> 00:07:03.958
I think this is where he wants us to go.

00:07:07.709 --> 00:07:08.831
This is a job.

00:07:10.676 --> 00:07:11.874
Dad wants us to work a job.

00:07:11.949 --> 00:07:13.645
Maybe we'll meet up with
him. Maybe he's there.

00:07:13.646 --> 00:07:14.718
Maybe he's not.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.961
May He could be sending us there
by ourselves to hunting thing.

00:07:16.962 --> 00:07:18.273
Who cares?

00:07:18.982 --> 00:07:20.878
If he wants us there,
it's good enough for me.

00:07:21.202 --> 00:07:22.923
This doesn't strike you as weird...

00:07:23.921 --> 00:07:24.894
The texting,

00:07:25.141 --> 00:07:26.413
The coordinates? Sam.

00:07:26.788 --> 00:07:28.933
Dad's telling us to go
somewhere. We're going.

00:07:49.915 --> 00:07:51.911
You're Daniel Gunderson,
right, you're cop?

00:07:52.086 --> 00:07:52.859
Yeah.

00:07:53.882 --> 00:07:54.730
I'm...

00:07:54.803 --> 00:07:56.075
Nigel Tufnel

00:07:56.125 --> 00:07:57.247
With the chicago tribune.

00:07:57.248 --> 00:07:58.794
Do you mind if I ask a couple questions

00:07:58.795 --> 00:07:59.842
About your partner?

00:07:59.843 --> 00:08:00.789
Yeah, I do.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:01.762
I'm just trying to have a beer here.

00:08:01.763 --> 00:08:04.082
I just want to hear
the story in your words.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.760
A week ago, my partner
was sitting in that chair,

00:08:07.159 --> 00:08:08.307
And now he's dead.

00:08:08.407 --> 00:08:09.554
Are you gonna ambush me here?

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:10.328
Sorry,

00:08:10.329 --> 00:08:11.924
But I need to know what happened.

00:08:12.049 --> 00:08:14.817
Heyn buddy! How about leaving
the poor guy alone, huh?!

00:08:15.151 --> 00:08:17.596
The man's an officer! Why don't
you show a little respect?!

00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:25.926
You didn't have to do that.

00:08:26.125 --> 00:08:27.298
Yeah, of course I did.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.327
That guy's a serious jerk.

00:08:29.552 --> 00:08:31.423
Let me buy you a beer, huh?

00:08:32.096 --> 00:08:33.094
Two?

00:08:36.712 --> 00:08:37.485
Thanks.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:43.997
You shoved me kind of
hard in there, buddy boy.

00:08:44.022 --> 00:08:45.519
I had to sell it, didn't I?

00:08:46.168 --> 00:08:47.365
It's method acting.

00:08:48.413 --> 00:08:49.236
Huh?

00:08:49.733 --> 00:08:50.505
Never mind.

00:08:50.506 --> 00:08:51.628
What did you find out from Gunderson?

00:08:51.728 --> 00:08:53.399
So, Walter Kelly was a good cop.

00:08:53.624 --> 00:08:55.220
Head of his class, even-Keeled.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:56.617
He had a bright future ahead of him.

00:08:56.618 --> 00:08:57.266
What about at home?

00:08:57.267 --> 00:08:59.235
He and his wife had a few
fights. Like everybody.

00:08:59.285 --> 00:09:00.757
But it was mostly smooth sailing.

00:09:00.907 --> 00:09:02.502
They were even talking
about having kids.

00:09:02.503 --> 00:09:05.246
All right, so how the kelly had some
deep see the crazy way in the bus

00:09:05.247 --> 00:09:06.619
Or something else did it to him. Right.

00:09:06.716 --> 00:09:08.462
What did Gunderson tell
you about the asylum?

00:09:09.585 --> 00:09:10.283
A lot.

00:09:35.303 --> 00:09:38.022
So, apparently, the cops
chased the kids here...

00:09:39.841 --> 00:09:41.362
Into the south wing.

00:09:43.433 --> 00:09:44.605
South wing, huh?

00:09:45.223 --> 00:09:46.745
Wait a second.

00:09:47.968 --> 00:09:49.864
South wing, south wing.

00:09:52.881 --> 00:09:54.403
"1972,

00:09:54.603 --> 00:09:56.464
Three kids broke into the south wing.

00:09:56.589 --> 00:09:58.061
Only one survived."

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:59.555
The way he tells it, one of his friends

00:09:59.556 --> 00:10:01.526
Went nuts and started
lighting up the place.

00:10:02.449 --> 00:10:04.095
So, whatever's going on,

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.741
South wing seems like the heart of it.

00:10:05.791 --> 00:10:07.363
Yeah, but if kids are
spelunking the asylum,

00:10:07.364 --> 00:10:09.180
Why aren't there a ton more deaths?

00:10:11.176 --> 00:10:13.097
It looks like the doors
are usually chained.

00:10:14.145 --> 00:10:15.817
They could have been
chained up for years.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.056
Yeah, to keep people out.

00:10:18.704 --> 00:10:20.351
Or to keep something in.

00:10:30.704 --> 00:10:33.049
Let me know if you see any
dead people, Haley Joel.

00:10:33.199 --> 00:10:34.321
Dude, enough.

00:10:35.219 --> 00:10:36.938
I'm serious. You've got
to be careful. Right.

00:10:36.939 --> 00:10:39.133
Ghosts are attracted to
that E.S.P. Thing you got.

00:10:39.134 --> 00:10:40.331
I told you, it's not E.S.P.

00:10:40.332 --> 00:10:42.550
I just have strange vibes, sometimes,

00:10:43.149 --> 00:10:43.823
Weird dreams.

00:10:43.824 --> 00:10:45.736
Yeah, whatever. Don't ask, don't tell.

00:10:45.961 --> 00:10:47.358
Do you get any reading
on that thing or not?

00:10:47.433 --> 00:10:49.354
No. Of course, it doesn't
mean nobody's home.

00:10:49.429 --> 00:10:51.674
Spirits can't appear
during certain hours of day.

00:10:51.699 --> 00:10:53.169
The freaks come out at night.

00:10:53.393 --> 00:10:54.366
Ya. Hey Sam

00:10:54.416 --> 00:10:55.937
Who do you think is a hotter psychic

00:10:56.012 --> 00:10:58.058
Patricia Arquette,
Jennifer Love Hewitt or you?

00:11:25.029 --> 00:11:26.002
Man.

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:28.597
Electroshock,

00:11:28.771 --> 00:11:31.413
Lobotomies. They did some
twisted stuff to these people,

00:11:31.638 --> 00:11:34.555
Kind of like my man
Jack in "cuckoo's nest."

00:11:38.443 --> 00:11:40.264
So, what do you think?

00:11:40.913 --> 00:11:42.534
Ghosts are possessing people?

00:11:43.183 --> 00:11:44.056
Maybe.

00:11:44.903 --> 00:11:47.897
Maybe it's more like Amityville
or the smurl haunting.

00:11:48.093 --> 00:11:50.389
Ah, spirits driving them insane,

00:11:51.012 --> 00:11:53.158
Kind of like my man
Jack in "the shining."

00:11:56.899 --> 00:11:57.869
Dean...

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:00.963
When are we going to talk about it?

00:12:01.063 --> 00:12:01.711
Talk about what?

00:12:01.736 --> 00:12:03.333
About the fact that dad's not here.

00:12:03.508 --> 00:12:05.454
Oh, uh, let's see, never.

00:12:05.455 --> 00:12:06.402
I'm being serious, man.

00:12:06.403 --> 00:12:07.229
So am I, sam.

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:09.698
Look. He sent us here. He
obviously wants us here.

00:12:09.897 --> 00:12:11.020
We'll just have to pick
up the search later.

00:12:11.021 --> 00:12:12.592
It doesn't matter what he wants.

00:12:12.593 --> 00:12:14.933
See, that attitude right there,

00:12:15.432 --> 00:12:16.954
That is why I always
got the extra cookie.

00:12:17.078 --> 00:12:18.176
Dad could be in trouble.

00:12:18.251 --> 00:12:19.773
We should be looking for him.

00:12:19.798 --> 00:12:22.616
We deserve some answers, Dean. I mean,
this is our family were talking about..

00:12:22.617 --> 00:12:24.035
I understand that, sam,

00:12:24.185 --> 00:12:25.207
But he's given us an order.

00:12:25.208 --> 00:12:26.904
So what ? We've got to
always follow dad's orders?

00:12:26.929 --> 00:12:28.251
Of course we do.

00:12:39.271 --> 00:12:41.018
Sanford Ellicott

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.263
You know what we got to do?

00:12:43.388 --> 00:12:45.478
We've got to find out
more about the south wing,

00:12:46.005 --> 00:12:47.551
See if something happened here.

00:13:04.103 --> 00:13:05.151
Sam Winchester?

00:13:06.199 --> 00:13:06.948
That's me.

00:13:07.022 --> 00:13:08.020
Come on in.

00:13:14.325 --> 00:13:16.723
Thanks again for see me last minute.

00:13:31.866 --> 00:13:32.964
Dr. Ellicott?

00:13:33.784 --> 00:13:34.982
Ellicott, that name.

00:13:35.256 --> 00:13:38.299
Wasn't there a dr. Sanford Ellicott?

00:13:38.698 --> 00:13:41.317
Yeah, he was a chief
psychiatrist somewhere.

00:13:41.318 --> 00:13:44.359
My father was chief of staff
at the old Roosevelt asylum.

00:13:44.484 --> 00:13:45.532
How did you know?

00:13:46.155 --> 00:13:49.198
Huh, well, I'm sort of
a local-History buff.

00:13:49.345 --> 00:13:53.137
Hey, wasn't there an incident
or something in the...

00:13:53.337 --> 00:13:55.233
In the hospital, I guess,
in the south wing, right?

00:13:55.282 --> 00:13:56.804
We're on your dollar, Sam.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:59.242
We're here to talk about you.

00:14:00.165 --> 00:14:02.235
Oh, okay, yeah, yeah, sure.

00:14:03.978 --> 00:14:05.101
So? So.

00:14:05.226 --> 00:14:06.373
How's things?

00:14:06.573 --> 00:14:08.918
Uh, things are good, doctor.

00:14:08.968 --> 00:14:09.816
Good.

00:14:10.016 --> 00:14:11.263
What you been doing?

00:14:12.109 --> 00:14:13.231
Uh...

00:14:13.854 --> 00:14:15.999
Same old. I've just been on a...

00:14:16.074 --> 00:14:18.095
On a road trip with my brother.

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.392
Was that fun?

00:14:21.461 --> 00:14:22.483
Loads.

00:14:23.032 --> 00:14:24.130
Um...

00:14:24.504 --> 00:14:25.677
You know... We...

00:14:26.873 --> 00:14:28.320
Met a lot of...

00:14:29.069 --> 00:14:30.191
Interesting people.

00:14:30.241 --> 00:14:30.990
Mm-Hmm.

00:14:31.141 --> 00:14:32.663
Did a lot of, uh...

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.357
A lot of interesting things.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.303
Uh...

00:14:38.376 --> 00:14:39.323
You know,

00:14:39.697 --> 00:14:40.795
What was it...

00:14:40.859 --> 00:14:42.780
Exactly that happened in the south wing?

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:43.778
I forget... Look,

00:14:43.928 --> 00:14:45.325
If you're a local-History buff,

00:14:45.372 --> 00:14:47.368
Then you know all about
the Roosevelt riot.

00:14:47.718 --> 00:14:48.466
The riot?

00:14:48.491 --> 00:14:50.711
Well, no, I know, I'm
just curious -- Sam.

00:14:51.459 --> 00:14:52.881
Let's cut the bull, shall we?

00:14:53.627 --> 00:14:55.124
You're avoiding the subject.

00:14:58.317 --> 00:14:59.216
What subject?

00:14:59.315 --> 00:15:00.164
You.

00:15:00.787 --> 00:15:02.384
Now, I'll make you a deal.

00:15:03.055 --> 00:15:05.249
I'll tell you all
about the Roosevelt riot

00:15:05.424 --> 00:15:07.819
If you tell me something
honest about yourself...

00:15:08.492 --> 00:15:09.515
Like, uh...

00:15:10.111 --> 00:15:12.107
This brother you're road-Tripping with.

00:15:12.606 --> 00:15:14.078
How do you feel about him?

00:15:25.812 --> 00:15:26.336
Dude.

00:15:26.436 --> 00:15:28.580
You were in there forever. What
the hell were you talking about?

00:15:28.927 --> 00:15:30.125
Just the hospital, you know.

00:15:30.199 --> 00:15:30.923
And?

00:15:30.998 --> 00:15:32.669
And the south wing,

00:15:32.769 --> 00:15:34.291
It's where they housed
the real hard cases,

00:15:34.341 --> 00:15:36.137
Psychotics, the criminally insane.

00:15:36.184 --> 00:15:36.933
Sounds cozy.

00:15:36.958 --> 00:15:39.203
Yeah, and one night in '64, they rioted,

00:15:39.402 --> 00:15:41.322
Attacked the staff, attacked each other.

00:15:41.397 --> 00:15:42.969
So, what, the patients
took over the asylum?

00:15:43.116 --> 00:15:44.638
Apparently. Any deaths?

00:15:44.938 --> 00:15:46.884
Some patients, some staff.

00:15:47.008 --> 00:15:48.156
I guess it was pretty gory.

00:15:48.157 --> 00:15:49.902
Some of the bodies were
never even recovered,

00:15:50.002 --> 00:15:52.023
Including our chief of staff, Ellicott.

00:15:52.024 --> 00:15:53.295
What do you mean "Never recovered"?

00:15:53.323 --> 00:15:54.645
Cops scoured every inch of the place,

00:15:54.695 --> 00:15:56.566
But I guess the patients must have...

00:15:57.713 --> 00:15:59.984
Stuffed the bodies somewhere hidden.

00:16:00.355 --> 00:16:01.453
That's grim. Ya.

00:16:01.927 --> 00:16:04.097
So they transferred all
the surviving patients

00:16:04.098 --> 00:16:05.644
And shut down the hospital for good.

00:16:05.645 --> 00:16:08.633
All right so the * we've got a bunch of
violent deaths and unrecovered bodies.

00:16:08.634 --> 00:16:10.179
Which could mean a
bunch of angry spirits.

00:16:10.454 --> 00:16:12.762
Not good times. Let's check
out the hospital tonight.

00:16:33.483 --> 00:16:34.930
Check this out.

00:16:36.152 --> 00:16:37.125
Creepy...

00:16:38.927 --> 00:16:40.224
Yet terrifying.

00:16:42.095 --> 00:16:43.716
I thought we were going to a movie.

00:16:44.364 --> 00:16:46.236
This is better. It's
like we're in a movie.

00:16:48.129 --> 00:16:49.900
I can't believe you call this a date.

00:16:52.791 --> 00:16:54.213
Come on. That'll be fine.

00:16:54.762 --> 00:16:56.083
That's look around.

00:16:56.682 --> 00:16:57.854
Come on!

00:17:04.815 --> 00:17:05.838
What was that? Ugh!

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:10.428
Hey, look.

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:12.072
Come on, let's check it out.

00:17:12.446 --> 00:17:13.893
I don't want to.

00:17:14.667 --> 00:17:15.390
Let's just go.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:16.712
Come on.

00:17:19.489 --> 00:17:20.412
Okay.

00:17:20.785 --> 00:17:22.008
Okay. You can wait here.

00:17:22.108 --> 00:17:23.355
Gavin, no.

00:17:23.455 --> 00:17:24.677
I'm just gonna be a minute.

00:17:26.124 --> 00:17:28.045
Nothing's gonna get you, I promise.

00:18:20.844 --> 00:18:21.817
Damn it.

00:18:25.888 --> 00:18:28.108
Hey, sweetie, couldn't take it, huh?

00:18:32.472 --> 00:18:33.345
Hey.

00:18:38.159 --> 00:18:40.379
Gavin, where are you?

00:18:42.757 --> 00:18:43.780
Gavin.

00:19:12.861 --> 00:19:13.984
Getting readings?

00:19:14.483 --> 00:19:15.480
No, big-Time.

00:19:15.705 --> 00:19:17.701
This place is orbing like crazy.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:23.736
There's probably multiple
spirits out and about.

00:19:23.782 --> 00:19:26.226
And if these unrecovered
bodies are causing the haunting?

00:19:26.227 --> 00:19:27.547
We got to find them and burn them.

00:19:27.597 --> 00:19:28.328
Just be careful.

00:19:28.329 --> 00:19:31.301
The only thing that makes me more
nervous than a pissed-Off spirit

00:19:31.788 --> 00:19:34.559
Is a pissed-Off spirit
of a psycho killer.

00:20:45.502 --> 00:20:46.237
Dean!

00:20:46.972 --> 00:20:47.594
Dean!

00:20:48.386 --> 00:20:49.206
Shotgun!

00:20:49.856 --> 00:20:50.677
Sam, get down!

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:01.750
That was weird.

00:21:01.948 --> 00:21:02.655
Yeah,

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:03.927
You're telling me.

00:21:05.905 --> 00:21:08.620
No, Dean, I mean, it was weird
that she didn't attack me.

00:21:08.711 --> 00:21:10.520
It looked pretty aggro
from where I was standing.

00:21:10.521 --> 00:21:11.765
She didn't hurt me.

00:21:11.849 --> 00:21:13.037
She didn't even try.

00:21:13.439 --> 00:21:15.786
So she didn't want to hurt
me, then what did she want?

00:21:44.843 --> 00:21:46.314
It's all right.We're
not going to hurt you.

00:21:48.152 --> 00:21:49.226
It's okay.

00:21:50.109 --> 00:21:50.788
What's your name?

00:21:50.816 --> 00:21:51.608
Katherine.

00:21:52.909 --> 00:21:53.785
Kat.

00:21:53.955 --> 00:21:54.689
Okay.

00:21:54.944 --> 00:21:55.990
I'm dean.This is sam.

00:21:55.991 --> 00:21:57.234
What are you doing here?

00:21:58.545 --> 00:22:00.355
My boyfriend, Gavin...

00:22:00.638 --> 00:22:01.684
Is he here?

00:22:02.284 --> 00:22:03.387
Somewhere.

00:22:04.065 --> 00:22:07.006
He thought it would be fun,
try and see some ghosts.

00:22:07.797 --> 00:22:09.522
I thought it was all just...

00:22:10.404 --> 00:22:11.394
You know...

00:22:12.129 --> 00:22:13.260
Pretend.

00:22:16.229 --> 00:22:17.332
I've seen things.

00:22:18.866 --> 00:22:20.759
I heard Gavin scream, and...

00:22:20.844 --> 00:22:22.512
All right, Kat, come on.

00:22:22.852 --> 00:22:24.774
Sam's gonna get you out of here.
Then we're gonna find your boyfriend.

00:22:24.792 --> 00:22:26.404
No, no.

00:22:27.507 --> 00:22:29.458
I'm not gonna leave without Gavin.

00:22:29.713 --> 00:22:31.013
I'm coming with you.

00:22:31.014 --> 00:22:33.055
It's no a joke around
here, okay. It's dangerous.

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:34.836
That's why I've got to find him.

00:22:36.476 --> 00:22:38.173
All right, I guess we're
gonna split up, then.

00:22:38.423 --> 00:22:39.356
Let's go.

00:22:43.654 --> 00:22:44.727
Gavin!

00:22:48.326 --> 00:22:49.316
Gavin!

00:22:52.483 --> 00:22:53.444
Gavin!

00:22:56.046 --> 00:22:57.063
Gavin!

00:22:57.437 --> 00:22:58.822
I've got a question for you.

00:22:59.218 --> 00:23:01.141
You've seen a lot of
horror movies, yeah?

00:23:01.367 --> 00:23:02.159
I guess so.

00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:04.025
Do me a favor. Next time you see one,

00:23:04.195 --> 00:23:05.241
Pay attention.

00:23:05.676 --> 00:23:07.288
When someone says a place is haunted,

00:23:07.571 --> 00:23:08.674
Don't go in.

00:23:23.435 --> 00:23:24.198
Gavin?

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:25.923
Hey, gavin.

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:28.949
Hey, it's okay. It's
okay. I'm here to help.

00:23:29.656 --> 00:23:30.362
Who are you?

00:23:30.363 --> 00:23:31.698
My name is Sam.

00:23:32.207 --> 00:23:33.536
We found your girlfriend.

00:23:34.017 --> 00:23:34.893
Kat? Yeah.

00:23:34.894 --> 00:23:36.052
Is she all right?

00:23:36.256 --> 00:23:38.473
She's worried about you. Are you okay?

00:23:40.143 --> 00:23:41.806
I was running. I, uh,

00:23:41.936 --> 00:23:43.012
I think I fell.

00:23:43.013 --> 00:23:44.382
You were running from what?

00:23:46.176 --> 00:23:47.381
There was...

00:23:47.903 --> 00:23:50.649
There was this girl. Her-Her face...

00:23:52.246 --> 00:23:53.388
It was all messed up.

00:23:53.389 --> 00:23:54.431
Okay, listen, listen,

00:23:54.432 --> 00:23:56.420
This girl, did she try to hurt you?

00:23:57.047 --> 00:23:59.101
What? No, she, uh...

00:23:59.915 --> 00:24:01.187
She what?

00:24:02.361 --> 00:24:03.535
She kissed me.

00:24:06.020 --> 00:24:08.857
Um, but she didn't hurt you physically?

00:24:09.052 --> 00:24:10.976
Dude, she kissed me.

00:24:11.627 --> 00:24:12.801
I'm scarred for life.

00:24:14.079 --> 00:24:15.677
Trust me, it could have been worse.

00:24:15.678 --> 00:24:17.340
And now, do you remember anything else?

00:24:17.764 --> 00:24:18.938
She, uh...

00:24:19.786 --> 00:24:21.742
Actually, she tried to
whisper something in my ear.

00:24:22.369 --> 00:24:23.249
What?

00:24:24.063 --> 00:24:25.596
I don't know. I ran like hell.

00:24:40.308 --> 00:24:42.232
You son of a bitch.

00:24:43.014 --> 00:24:44.873
It's all right. I've got a lighter.

00:24:47.991 --> 00:24:49.979
Ow. You're hurting my arm.

00:24:50.990 --> 00:24:52.197
What are you talking about?

00:25:00.997 --> 00:25:03.670
Let me out!Please!

00:25:08.585 --> 00:25:10.748
Kat, hang on!

00:25:38.352 --> 00:25:39.297
What's going on?

00:25:39.298 --> 00:25:40.454
She's inside with one of them.

00:25:40.455 --> 00:25:41.694
Help me!

00:25:41.759 --> 00:25:42.509
Kat!

00:25:42.510 --> 00:25:43.781
Get me out of here!

00:25:43.782 --> 00:25:45.693
Kat, it's not gonna hurt you.

00:25:46.215 --> 00:25:48.856
Listen to me. You have to
face it. You have to calm down.

00:25:48.857 --> 00:25:50.005
She's got to what?

00:25:50.006 --> 00:25:50.918
I have to what?

00:25:50.919 --> 00:25:53.754
These spirits, they don't try to
hurt, they're trying to communicate.

00:25:53.755 --> 00:25:55.352
You've got to listen to.
You've got to face it.

00:25:55.353 --> 00:25:56.297
You face it.

00:25:56.298 --> 00:25:57.928
No. It's the only way you're
gonna get out of there.

00:25:57.929 --> 00:25:58.709
No!

00:25:58.710 --> 00:25:59.883
Look at it.That's all.

00:25:59.948 --> 00:26:01.285
Come on.You can do it.

00:26:22.831 --> 00:26:23.581
Kat?

00:26:25.473 --> 00:26:27.103
Now, I hope you're right about this.

00:26:29.099 --> 00:26:30.306
Yeah, me, too.

00:26:40.232 --> 00:26:41.372
Oh, Kat.

00:26:46.596 --> 00:26:47.966
1, 3, 7.

00:26:48.716 --> 00:26:49.759
Sorry?

00:26:51.096 --> 00:26:52.727
It whispered in my ear

00:26:53.118 --> 00:26:54.258
1, 3, 7.

00:26:55.243 --> 00:26:56.710
Room number.

00:27:00.004 --> 00:27:02.565
All right. So if these spirits
aren't trying to hurt anyone.

00:27:02.566 --> 00:27:04.131
Then what are they trying to do?

00:27:04.457 --> 00:27:05.729
Maybe that's what they've
been trying to tell us.

00:27:05.730 --> 00:27:06.869
I guess we'll find out.

00:27:07.554 --> 00:27:08.499
All right.

00:27:11.147 --> 00:27:12.028
So,

00:27:12.029 --> 00:27:14.245
Now, you guys ready to leave this place?

00:27:14.767 --> 00:27:15.974
That's an understatement.

00:27:16.007 --> 00:27:17.017
Okay.

00:27:17.441 --> 00:27:18.843
You get them out of here.

00:27:19.044 --> 00:27:20.773
I'm gonna gofind room 137.

00:27:29.742 --> 00:27:32.610
So, how do you guys know
about all this ghost stuff?

00:27:33.850 --> 00:27:35.708
It's kind of our job.

00:27:36.758 --> 00:27:38.715
Why would anyone want a job like that?

00:27:41.128 --> 00:27:43.247
I had a crappy guidance counselor.

00:27:45.503 --> 00:27:47.720
And Dean? He's your boss?

00:27:50.035 --> 00:27:50.916
No.

00:28:35.028 --> 00:28:36.038
All right.

00:28:36.299 --> 00:28:37.930
I think we have a small problem.

00:28:38.515 --> 00:28:39.558
Let's break it down.

00:28:39.721 --> 00:28:40.732
I don't think that's gonna work.

00:28:40.862 --> 00:28:41.743
Then a window.

00:28:41.744 --> 00:28:42.395
They're barred.

00:28:42.396 --> 00:28:44.091
How are we supposed to get out?

00:28:46.079 --> 00:28:47.807
That's the point. We're not.

00:28:48.368 --> 00:28:49.673
There's something in here.

00:28:49.803 --> 00:28:51.009
It doesn't want us to leave.

00:28:53.357 --> 00:28:54.238
Those patients.

00:28:54.303 --> 00:28:55.249
No.

00:28:55.770 --> 00:28:56.879
Something else.

00:29:22.635 --> 00:29:25.145
This is why I get paid the big bucks.

00:29:31.694 --> 00:29:33.031
"Patients journal."

00:29:49.226 --> 00:29:51.834
All work and no play makes Dr. Ellicott,

00:29:51.972 --> 00:29:53.961
A very dull boy.

00:30:01.892 --> 00:30:03.681
Right. I've looked everywhere.

00:30:03.963 --> 00:30:05.058
There's no other way out.

00:30:05.434 --> 00:30:06.419
So, what the hell are we gonna do?

00:30:06.482 --> 00:30:08.036
For starters, we're not gonna panic.

00:30:08.176 --> 00:30:09.240
Why the hell not?

00:30:11.775 --> 00:30:12.401
Hey.

00:30:12.448 --> 00:30:13.479
Sam, it's me.

00:30:13.949 --> 00:30:15.654
I see it. It's coming at me.

00:30:15.972 --> 00:30:16.691
Where are you?

00:30:16.692 --> 00:30:17.771
I'm in the basement. Hurry up!

00:30:17.802 --> 00:30:18.710
I'm on my way.

00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:21.041
All right. Can either
of you handle a shotgun?

00:30:21.448 --> 00:30:22.402
What?! No!

00:30:22.856 --> 00:30:23.560
I can.

00:30:25.269 --> 00:30:27.052
My dad took me skeet
shooting a couple times.

00:30:27.099 --> 00:30:27.944
Oh, I heard.

00:30:28.085 --> 00:30:29.117
It's loaded with rock salt.

00:30:29.164 --> 00:30:30.134
Now, it might not kill a spirit,

00:30:30.181 --> 00:30:31.683
But it will repel it,
so if you see something,

00:30:31.840 --> 00:30:32.340
Shoot.

00:30:32.356 --> 00:30:33.013
Okay.

00:30:33.248 --> 00:30:33.858
Okay.

00:30:40.574 --> 00:30:41.371
Dean!

00:30:59.942 --> 00:31:00.802
Dean!

00:32:01.904 --> 00:32:02.734
Dean?

00:32:30.292 --> 00:32:31.575
Don't be afraid.

00:32:31.919 --> 00:32:33.421
I'm going to make you all better.

00:32:40.726 --> 00:32:41.774
Hey, Gavin.

00:32:43.515 --> 00:32:44.219
Yeah?

00:32:45.955 --> 00:32:47.676
If we make it out of here alive,

00:32:48.865 --> 00:32:50.383
We are so breaking up.

00:32:53.822 --> 00:32:54.869
Did you hear that?

00:32:55.041 --> 00:32:56.105
Something's coming.

00:32:59.766 --> 00:33:01.159
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:33:01.769 --> 00:33:03.099
Don't shoot! It's me!

00:33:03.349 --> 00:33:05.012
Sorry. Sorry.

00:33:05.591 --> 00:33:06.858
Son of a...

00:33:11.191 --> 00:33:12.443
What are you still doing here?

00:33:12.714 --> 00:33:13.668
Where's Sam?

00:33:13.981 --> 00:33:15.420
He went to the basement. You called him.

00:33:16.265 --> 00:33:17.063
I didn't call him.

00:33:17.193 --> 00:33:18.319
His cellphone rang.

00:33:18.616 --> 00:33:19.570
He said it was you.

00:33:21.604 --> 00:33:22.589
Basement, huh?

00:33:26.905 --> 00:33:27.749
All right.

00:33:28.860 --> 00:33:29.846
Watch yourselves.

00:33:32.035 --> 00:33:33.130
And watch out for me.

00:33:39.354 --> 00:33:40.152
Sammy?

00:33:41.889 --> 00:33:43.140
Sam, you down here?

00:33:44.032 --> 00:33:44.845
Sam!

00:33:47.348 --> 00:33:48.244
Sam!

00:33:50.576 --> 00:33:51.311
Man...

00:33:52.093 --> 00:33:53.705
Answer me when I'm calling you.

00:33:54.268 --> 00:33:54.847
You all right?

00:33:54.848 --> 00:33:55.911
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:33:56.052 --> 00:33:57.474
You know that wasn't
me who called, right?

00:33:57.572 --> 00:33:59.558
Yeah, I know. I think
something lured me down here.

00:33:59.559 --> 00:34:00.920
I think I know who

00:34:01.139 --> 00:34:01.999
Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:02.441 --> 00:34:04.647
That's what the spirits have been trying
to tell us. You haven't seen him, have you?

00:34:04.741 --> 00:34:05.555
No.

00:34:05.743 --> 00:34:06.697
How do you knowit was him?

00:34:06.698 --> 00:34:08.042
Because I found his logbook.

00:34:08.074 --> 00:34:10.607
Apparently, he was
experimenting on his patients.

00:34:11.097 --> 00:34:12.223
Awful stuff.

00:34:12.254 --> 00:34:13.929
Makes lobotomies look
like a couple of aspirin.

00:34:13.930 --> 00:34:15.571
But it was the patients who rioted.

00:34:15.572 --> 00:34:17.324
Yeah. They were rioting
against Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:18.575 --> 00:34:22.052
Dr. Feelgood was working on some
sort of extreme-Rage therapy.

00:34:22.053 --> 00:34:24.383
He thought if he could get his
patients to vent their anger,

00:34:24.493 --> 00:34:25.776
Then they'd be cured of it.

00:34:26.167 --> 00:34:27.466
Instead it only made
them worse and worse

00:34:27.467 --> 00:34:28.717
And angrier and angrier.

00:34:28.921 --> 00:34:30.360
I'm thinking, what if his spirit

00:34:30.579 --> 00:34:31.799
Is doing the same thing?

00:34:32.034 --> 00:34:32.801
To the cop,

00:34:32.915 --> 00:34:34.291
The kids in the '70s

00:34:34.604 --> 00:34:36.966
Making them so angry
they become homicidal.

00:34:38.046 --> 00:34:38.718
Come on.

00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:40.690
We've got to find his
bones and torch them.

00:34:41.190 --> 00:34:42.035
How?

00:34:42.355 --> 00:34:43.669
The police never found his body.

00:34:43.731 --> 00:34:46.454
The logbook said he had some
hidden procedure room down here

00:34:46.455 --> 00:34:48.596
Somewhere where he'd
work on his patients. So,

00:34:48.742 --> 00:34:50.541
If I was a patient, I'd
drag his ass down here

00:34:50.542 --> 00:34:51.902
Do a little work on myself.

00:34:51.949 --> 00:34:53.357
I don't know.It sounds kind of...

00:34:53.420 --> 00:34:54.139
Of crazy?

00:34:54.140 --> 00:34:54.655
Yeah.

00:34:54.656 --> 00:34:56.126
Yeah, exactly.

00:35:12.124 --> 00:35:13.376
I told you I looked everywhere.

00:35:13.377 --> 00:35:15.081
I didn't find a hidden room.

00:35:15.457 --> 00:35:17.037
Well, that's why they call it hidden.

00:35:19.967 --> 00:35:21.031
You hear that?

00:35:22.470 --> 00:35:23.378
What?

00:35:34.243 --> 00:35:35.494
There's a door here.

00:35:38.873 --> 00:35:39.796
Dean.

00:35:45.202 --> 00:35:46.782
Step back from the door.

00:35:51.735 --> 00:35:53.081
Sam, put the gun down.

00:35:53.456 --> 00:35:54.614
Is that an order?

00:35:56.288 --> 00:35:57.962
That's more of a friendly request.

00:35:57.963 --> 00:36:00.262
'Cause I'm getting pretty
tired of taking your orders.

00:36:01.893 --> 00:36:02.988
I knew it.

00:36:03.583 --> 00:36:04.741
Ellicott did something
to you, didn't he?

00:36:04.742 --> 00:36:05.961
For once in your life,

00:36:06.384 --> 00:36:07.291
Shut your mouth.

00:36:07.292 --> 00:36:08.689
What are you gonna do, sam?

00:36:09.215 --> 00:36:10.958
The gun's filled with rock salt.

00:36:11.150 --> 00:36:12.182
It's not gonna kill me.

00:36:15.545 --> 00:36:16.171
No.

00:36:16.468 --> 00:36:17.376
But it'll hurt like hell.

00:36:25.369 --> 00:36:26.167
Sam.

00:36:26.791 --> 00:36:28.372
We've got to burn Ellicott's bones,

00:36:28.403 --> 00:36:29.780
And all this will be over,

00:36:30.145 --> 00:36:31.365
And you'll be back to normal.

00:36:31.537 --> 00:36:32.585
I am normal.

00:36:33.618 --> 00:36:35.229
I'm just telling the
truth for the first time.

00:36:35.730 --> 00:36:37.451
I mean, why are we even here?

00:36:38.249 --> 00:36:40.944
'Cause you're following dad's
orders like a good little soldier?

00:36:41.038 --> 00:36:43.556
'Cause you always do what
he says without question?

00:36:43.854 --> 00:36:45.856
Are you that desperate for his approval?

00:36:46.060 --> 00:36:47.499
This isn't you talking, Sam.

00:36:47.567 --> 00:36:49.163
That's the difference
between you and me.

00:36:49.382 --> 00:36:51.258
I have a mind of my own.

00:36:51.508 --> 00:36:53.276
I'm not pathetic like you.

00:36:53.277 --> 00:36:55.357
So what are you gonna do?
Huh. You gonna kill me?

00:36:55.404 --> 00:36:58.330
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:36:55.404 --> 00:36:58.330
You know, I am sick of
doing what you tell me to do.

00:36:58.820 --> 00:37:00.714
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:37:00.822 --> 00:37:02.653
Than we were six months ago.

00:37:04.534 --> 00:37:05.817
Well, then here.

00:37:06.067 --> 00:37:07.898
Let me make it easier for you.

00:37:10.088 --> 00:37:11.058
Come on.

00:37:11.246 --> 00:37:12.200
Take it.

00:37:12.554 --> 00:37:15.401
Real bullets are gonna work a hell
of a lot better than rock salt.

00:37:16.464 --> 00:37:17.356
Take it.

00:37:29.236 --> 00:37:30.738
You hate me that much?

00:37:32.365 --> 00:37:34.196
You think you can kill your own brother?

00:37:37.074 --> 00:37:38.419
Then go ahead.

00:37:39.640 --> 00:37:40.907
Pull the trigger.

00:37:47.265 --> 00:37:48.485
Do it!

00:38:06.025 --> 00:38:08.372
Man, I'm not gonna give
you a loaded pistol.

00:38:15.849 --> 00:38:17.085
Sorry, Sammy.

00:39:20.516 --> 00:39:21.985
Oh, that's just gross.

00:39:31.050 --> 00:39:32.130
Soak it up.

00:39:45.006 --> 00:39:46.414
Don't be afraid.

00:39:47.247 --> 00:39:48.640
I'm going to help you.

00:39:48.749 --> 00:39:50.580
I'm going to make you all better.

00:40:41.764 --> 00:40:43.626
You're not gonna try
and kill me, are you?

00:40:46.536 --> 00:40:47.365
No.

00:40:48.198 --> 00:40:49.054
Good.

00:40:50.435 --> 00:40:52.391
'Cause that would be awkward.

00:40:58.589 --> 00:40:59.731
Thanks, guys.

00:41:00.060 --> 00:41:01.248
Yeah, thanks.

00:41:01.639 --> 00:41:03.704
No more haunted asylums, okay?

00:41:11.132 --> 00:41:12.102
Hey, Dean.

00:41:13.493 --> 00:41:15.074
I' sorry, man. I

00:41:16.325 --> 00:41:18.187
said some awful thingsback there.

00:41:18.755 --> 00:41:20.022
You remember all that?

00:41:20.413 --> 00:41:21.274
Yeah.

00:41:22.964 --> 00:41:25.841
It's like I couldn't control
it, but I didn't mean it

00:41:26.248 --> 00:41:27.218
Any of it.

00:41:27.907 --> 00:41:28.861
You didn't, huh?

00:41:29.883 --> 00:41:30.900
No. Of course, not.

00:41:33.768 --> 00:41:35.348
Do we need to talk about this?

00:41:36.365 --> 00:41:37.241
No.

00:41:37.327 --> 00:41:40.103
I'm not really in the sharing
and caring kind of mood.

00:41:40.709 --> 00:41:42.258
I just want to get some sleep.

00:41:57.571 --> 00:41:58.431
Dean.

00:42:06.068 --> 00:42:06.928
Hello.

00:42:09.932 --> 00:42:10.652
Dad?

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.436
